{"path":"ranges/enumerate_view/iterator/operator_cmp","title":"operator==,<=>(ranges::enumerate_view::iterator)","titleHtml":"operator==,&lt;=&gt;<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(ranges::enumerate_view::<i>iterator</i>)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/enumerate_view/iterator/operator_cmp","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Compares the underlying iterators. Let pos_ be the underlying index.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; operator<span class=\"sy1\">==</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> y <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/compare/strong_ordering\"><span class=\"kw2678\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strong_ordering</span></span></a><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; operator<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;=&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> y <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Compares the underlying <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/enumerate_view/iterator\">iterators</a>. Let <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/enumerate_view/iterator#Data_members\"><code><i>pos_</i></code></a> be the underlying index.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> x.<span class=\"me1\">pos_</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> y.<span class=\"me1\">pos_</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> x.<span class=\"me1\">pos_</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;=&gt;</span> y.<span class=\"me1\">pos_</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>These functions are not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when <code>std::ranges::enumerate_view::<i>iterator</i>&lt;Const&gt;</code> is an associated class of the arguments.\n</p><p>The <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>, and <code>!=</code> operators are <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/operators#Comparison_operators\">synthesized</a> from <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operator<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;=&gt;</span></span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operator<span class=\"sy1\">==</span></span> respectively.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x, y\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> iterators to compare\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Result of comparison.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/enumerate_view/sentinel/operator_cmp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator==</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(C++23)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   compares a sentinel with an iterator returned from <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/enumerate_view/begin\"><code>enumerate_view::begin</code></a>  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/enumerate_view","title":"std::ranges::views::enumerate, std::ranges::enumerate_view"},{"path":"ranges/enumerate_view/iterator","title":"std::ranges::enumerate_view<V>::iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"operator==,<=>(ranges::enumerate_view::iterator)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++23. Compares the underlying iterators. Let pos_ be the underlying index."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"x, y"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Result of comparison."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator==","note":"compares a sentinel with an iterator returned from enumerate_view::begin"}]}]},"standards":["C++23"],"wordCount":122,"codeBlockCount":0}
